          "reproduction": "grep -rn \"squash\\|rebase\" .gitleaksignore docs/ops/*.md docs/policy/*.md -> the condition appears in no operator-facing record; it exists only as the criterion text in docs/ops/cross-review/packages/prompt-refiner-confirmatory-shadow-v4-integration-v4/task.json:8 and its copies under that package's records/. That the omission is load-bearing is shown by the repository itself: .gitleaksignore:27-28 records that the scheduled scan failed precisely because a pinned introducing commit was outside the scanned range; .github/workflows/daily-security-audit.yml:49-57 checks out with fetch-depth: 0 and scans full history, and lines 405-430 fail the job on that outcome; docs/ops/tomverse-chat-progress.md:1034 records a prior PR to develop being squash merged. Fix: add one line to the block, e.g. \"Valid only while commits 26aeecb..cb53fd0 remain in history -- merge this PR with a merge commit; never squash or rebase it.\", then re-run `node --conditions=react-server --import tsx --test tests/gitleaksAllowlist.test.mjs` (comment lines are skipped, so the format test still passes).",
